  "title": "# Build: follow-amber-switch (Current profile) - small ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, vo…",
  "asked": "# Build: follow-amber-switch (Current profile) - small ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"Make a widget that can go in the banner that is a switch which makes it automatically go to you when you mention something. You don't have to be asked to go to it. If you just mention something casually, it will go to that screen.\" Book to a free named agent (Snap Sully, else Janitor Joey). Register id `follow-amber-switch` in the `current` profile + banner entry + What Brett said block. ## Do - A **Follow Amber banner widget**: a compact switch chip ('Follow Amber' + on/off, Amber's avatar) that flips the existing Follow Amber state (follow-amber plugin, #280: follow_amber_switch / followAmber.enabled shared key from claude-settings #275 - reuse, don't add a second flag). Shows live state (synced across consoles/devices), a small pulse when Amber just opened something, and the last thing she opened (tap = reopen, long-press = recent list from follow_amber_recent). - Installed **in the console banner by default**, and available as a `hook@1` widget for any banner/toolbar (Molly's shared banner region too). Right-click/long-press -> Follow Amber settings. - Make console_show's description/tool guidance say: when Follow Amber is on, call it on ANY mention of a console screen, settings tab, build, plugin, PR or UI Review item - casual mentions included, no request needed. Also add a `followAmber.casual` note in Claude settings ('open things Amber mentions even in passing', default on) that sessions read. - Small and focused; type-check; one phone screenshot filed to UI Review (non-blocking); PR; merge when CI is green; redeploy console. Don't leave tsc/vite/playwright running. Report `_claude/builds/reports/follow-amber-switch.md`. Commits clean and professional. ## ADDENDUM 1 (Brett, voice) - REPLACES the new-widget part Brett: \"Is there already an Amber status widget?\" -> the **Claude badge** (banner, 'The AI connection badge', plugin claude-badge). \"You know how it shows green now? If Follow Amber's on, do a faded... make it two-tone.\" - **No new widget.** Put Follow Amber into the existing **Claude badge**: tap = toggle Follow Amber (keep the badge's current tap behaviour on long-press / context menu, or as a menu item - don't lose anything it does today). - **Two-tone when Follow Amber is on**: the badge keeps its connection colour (green = connected, etc.) and gets a second, faded tone (e.g. diagonal or half split / soft gradient with a lighter tint of the theme accent) so it's obviously different from plain green. Off = today's single colour. Uses theme tokens (works in every theme), smooth transition, tooltip/label says 'Follow Amber on/off'. Colours/style of the second tone settable in Claude badge settings. - The rest of the brief still applies (pulse when Amber opens something, last-opened on long-press menu, casual-mention guidance, shared followAmber.enabled key). ## ADDENDUM 2 (Brett, voice) Brett: \"The Claude badge, and some type of animation on the colors.\" - When Follow Amber is on, the two tones **animate**: default = a slow, smooth shimmer/gradient sweep between the connection colour and the faded tone (a few seconds per loop, subtle, never flashing). A brighter quick pulse when Amber opens something. - Claude badge settings: animation style (sweep / breathe / rotate / none), speed, intensity. Respect the OS 'reduce motion' setting (fall back to static two-tone). Cheap CSS animation, no JS timers. ## ADDENDUM 3 (Brett, voice) Brett: \"Give me a bunch of options for that animation. Also give me like 15 different badge options to choose from.\" - **Animation options** (picker with live preview, per state: Follow on / Amber just opened something / connecting / error): at least 10, e.g. sweep, breathe, rotate (conic), shimmer, ripple, glow pulse, wave, orbit dot, heartbeat, aurora gradient, sparkle, none. Speed, intensity, colours (from theme tokens or custom), loop vs once. - **~15 badge looks** as hot-swappable…",
